{
  "rationale": "The plant G models the robot's perception and actuation possibilities in a small grid world, including all motion and perception events, and allows all eight controllable actions somewhere. The specification E enforces safe, obstacle-aware movement, ensures move_backward is only used for front-obstacle recovery, prioritizes push for object progress, and requires the robot to stop only after all objects are in the red area. Recovery is brief and conservative, and forward progress resumes as soon as possible.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model plant G with states for clear, obstacle, pushing, and goal-detection, enabling all controllable actions somewhere and allowing all uncontrollable events from every state.",
    "Specification E constrains recovery, ensures push is prioritized for object progress, restricts move_backward to dedicated recovery, and enforces stop only after detect_object_red."
  ],
